Comment (src/components/system/ActiveSystemSelector.vue:92):
**[Must-fix] Header switcher requests the SSP list for users without ssp:read**

`loadPlans()` runs on every layout mount and every dropdown open, with no permission check. The API guards `GET /api/oscal/system-security-plans` with `guard.Read()`, so a user without `ssp:read` gets a 403 on every page load. That triggers the global "Permission denied" toast and a permissions re-hydrate. Before this PR the nav hid "Manage Systems" from these users. Reproduced: with `can()` returning false, the request is still sent.

**Why:** The switcher is in the layout, so for users without ssp:read every page shows a permission-denied toast for an action they never took.
**Fix:** Check `can(RESOURCES.SSP, ACTIONS.READ)` before calling `loadPlans()` (on mount and in `@show`). Since `can()` is optimistic until permissions load, also re-run it once the permission store has loaded. Without read access, hide the switcher or show it read-only and disabled. Add a spec for the denied case.
**Severity basis:** no rule matched; decision tree: wrong behaviour or missing companion change.

<sub>ccf-review · 39b9d1b3f40b · rules@992d25d050e9</sub>
Replies:
**lisa implementation guidance:** ActiveSystemSelector.vue: add `const canRead = computed(() => can(RESOURCES.SSP, ACTIONS.READ))`. Return early from loadPlans() when !canRead. Replace onMounted(loadPlans) with `watch(() => [canRead.value, permissionsStore.loaded], () => { if (canRead.value) loadPlans(); }, { immediate: true })` (usePermissionsStore exposes `loaded`), so a denial that arrives after hydration cancels the optimistic fetch and a later grant still loads. Render the component's root with v-if="canRead". Spec in ActiveSystemSelector.spec.ts: with the usePermissions mock returning false, get is never called and the select isn't rendered. Make the existing mock switchable per test.

